# OpenSearch: full-text search and faceted aggregations

Two Go services using the official `github.com/opensearch-project/opensearch-go/v5` client over verified HTTPS, seeded with 40 real public records from the **Washington State Department of Licensing Electric Vehicle Population Data** (`https://data.wa.gov/Transportation/Electric-Vehicle-Population-Data/f6w7-q2d2`).

- `ev-indexer` creates `ev-vehicles` with explicit `text`, `keyword`, and `integer` mappings (`number_of_shards: 1`, `number_of_replicas: 0`) and bulk-indexes all 40 EV registrations with deterministic document IDs.
- `ev-searcher` runs three query shapes every 8 seconds: a typo-tolerant BM25 `multi_match` (`"tesal model"`), a `bool` query separating scoring (`must`) from cached filters (`filter`), and faceted aggregations (`terms` by make + `range` buckets by electric range).

## Try this

- Watch both apps index and query:
  ```sh
  bb up
  bb logs ev-indexer
  bb logs ev-searcher -f
  ```
- Open `bb serve`, click `opensearch`, and view the **Indices** tab to see `ev-vehicles` turn `green` with 40 docs.
- Query the REST API directly from your host using the `host: true` URL shown by `bb status` and credentials from `bb creds opensearch`:
  ```sh
  curl --cacert "$(bb ca --host --pem >/tmp/bb-host-ca.pem && echo /tmp/bb-host-ca.pem)" \
    -u "admin:<password>" \
    "https://opensearch.{{.Experiment}}.localhost:<port>/ev-vehicles/_search?q=make:TESLA&pretty"
  ```
- Edit `cmd/ev-searcher/main.go` to add a `city` terms aggregation or filter by `model_year >= 2020`, then run `bb up` to rebuild and watch the new output.

## Break this

- **Violate an explicit mapping:** Send a document with `"electric_range": "three hundred"` to `ev-vehicles/_doc/bad-type` and observe OpenSearch reject the write with `mapper_parsing_exception` instead of corrupting numeric sorting.
- **Break green health on one node:** Update `number_of_replicas` to `1` on `ev-vehicles` via `PUT /ev-vehicles/_settings` and inspect the **Indices** tab — the cluster drops to `yellow` with 1 unassigned replica shard because OpenSearch will not place a replica on the same node as its primary.
